# From "One-Year Patterning" (Wave IV - Adventure, CD1-1) -- the same
# build-and-release method as patterning.gws, but every pattern is explicitly
# set one year ahead of the date the exercise is used. Condensed the same way:
# one full statement of the method, then the seven subjects against it.

@segment  one-year-patterning
@title    One-Year Patterning
@levels   F12
@duration ~4m

say From Focus 12, you'll create new patterns in your total being -- each one, as it will be one year from today.
pause 6
say For each: think of the pattern as already complete, one year ahead, an active reality of your total self. Build it. Make it stronger, more and more. Then release it, and let it flow out strongly into every part of your expanded awareness, in every direction.
pause 10
say First, your physical body, one year from today. Build the pattern.
pause 10
say Release it.
pause 6
say Now your mental self, one year ahead. Build it.
pause 10
say Release it.
pause 6
say Now your emotional self, one year ahead. Build it.
pause 10
say Release it.
pause 6
say Now your greater self, as you'll be one year from today. Build it.
pause 10
say Release it.
pause 6
say Now where you'll be, one year from today. Build the pattern.
pause 10
say Release it.
pause 6
say Now what you'll be doing, one year from today. Build it.
pause 10
say Release it.
pause 6
say Now what you'll have achieved, one year from today. Build it.
pause 10
say Release it.
pause 6
say You've created the total pattern -- who and how you'll be, one year ahead. Relax, and feel calm and comfortable.
pause 8
